<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Introduction on FAIRDataPipeline</title><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/</link><description>Recent content in Introduction on FAIRDataPipeline</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/standard_api/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/standard_api/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="standardised-data-type-api"&gt;Standardised data type API&lt;a class="anchor" href="#standardised-data-type-api"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Unless otherwise specified this document uses the “current” metadata scheme defined in the &amp;ldquo;Metadata and data representation” document. You do not need to have read that document to be able to read and understand (the majority of) this one.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The standardised data type API is defined more in terms of file formats than it is in terms of data types. There are two file formats: parameter files, and hdf5 files. Parameter files store “small” parameter data in toml format, representing individual parameters. HDF5 files are used to store structured data, encoded either as “arrays” or “tables”. Both formats are described in more detail below, alongside API functions used to interact with them.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/file_api/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/file_api/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="file-api"&gt;File API&lt;a class="anchor" href="#file-api"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="the-file-api-manages-file-access-provenance-and-metadata"&gt;The file API manages file access, provenance, and metadata&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-file-api-manages-file-access-provenance-and-metadata"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The API is accessed as a &amp;ldquo;session&amp;rdquo;. All reads and writes are recorded and logged into a file when the session closes. Files are identified by their metadata, though the metadata is handled differently for reads (where the files are expected to exist) and writes (where they typically do not), described in more detail below.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The file API behaviour is entirely determined by a yaml configuration file (referred to here as a “config.yaml” file, and described below) provided at initialisation. This configuration file defines the “data directory” that the file API should interact with. That directory must contain a file called “metadata.yaml”, described below, that defines the metadata associated with the files in the data directory. The data directory and the metadata.yaml file can be automatically created by a &lt;a href="https://github.com/ScottishCovidResponse/data_pipeline_api/tree/master/data_pipeline_api/registry" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;download script&lt;/a&gt; which reads the config.yaml file and downloads appropriate data and metadata.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Schema Description</title><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/schema/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/schema/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="schema-description"&gt;Schema Description&lt;a class="anchor" href="#schema-description"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The FAIR data registry schema records the data and the code of a modelling pipeline, and how they are connected, so that every result can be traced back to the code run that produced it and the inputs that it read.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every table is available through the registry&amp;rsquo;s REST API (&lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;/api/data_product/&lt;/code&gt;), where the description of each table lists its fields.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="data"&gt;Data&lt;a class="anchor" href="#data"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;pre class="mermaid" style="background-color: white"&gt;graph LR;&#10; EO(ExternalObject) -- original_store --&amp;gt; SL(StorageLocation)&#10; DP(DataProduct) -- external_object --&amp;gt; EO&#10; DP -- namespace --&amp;gt; NS(Namespace)&#10; DP -- object --&amp;gt; O(Object)&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DataProduct&lt;/strong&gt;: A dataset that is used by or generated by a model, identified by its &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;version&lt;/code&gt; (semantic versioning) and &lt;code&gt;Namespace&lt;/code&gt;. Once registered, its name, version, object and namespace cannot be changed.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Namespace&lt;/strong&gt;: A way to group &lt;code&gt;DataProduct&lt;/code&gt;s, for example by the organisation that produces them, with a unique &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;full_name&lt;/code&gt; and an optional &lt;code&gt;website&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ExternalObject&lt;/strong&gt;: Data that comes from somewhere other than the pipeline, such as a published dataset or paper. It is identified by an &lt;code&gt;identifier&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt; a DOI), or by an &lt;code&gt;alternate_identifier&lt;/code&gt; with its &lt;code&gt;alternate_identifier_type&lt;/code&gt;, together with its &lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;version&lt;/code&gt;, so a new release of a source is a new &lt;code&gt;ExternalObject&lt;/code&gt;. It also records the &lt;code&gt;release_date&lt;/code&gt;, whether it is a primary source (&lt;code&gt;primary_not_supplement&lt;/code&gt;), and optionally the &lt;code&gt;original_store&lt;/code&gt; it was copied from. Each &lt;code&gt;DataProduct&lt;/code&gt; registered from it points to it through &lt;code&gt;external_object&lt;/code&gt;, so one &lt;code&gt;ExternalObject&lt;/code&gt; can have several &lt;code&gt;DataProduct&lt;/code&gt;s.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="code-runs"&gt;Code runs&lt;a class="anchor" href="#code-runs"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;pre class="mermaid" style="background-color: white"&gt;graph LR;&#10; CR(CodeRun) -- code_repo --&amp;gt; O1(Object)&#10; CR -- model_config --&amp;gt; O2(Object)&#10; CR -- submission_script --&amp;gt; O3(Object)&#10; CR -- inputs --&amp;gt; OC1(ObjectComponent)&#10; CR -- outputs --&amp;gt; OC2(ObjectComponent)&#10; CRR(CodeRepoRelease) -- object --&amp;gt; O1&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CodeRun&lt;/strong&gt;: A run of a model, with its &lt;code&gt;run_date&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;uuid&lt;/code&gt;. It points to the &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;s for the code repository (&lt;code&gt;code_repo&lt;/code&gt;), the working configuration (&lt;code&gt;model_config&lt;/code&gt;) and the submission script, and lists the &lt;code&gt;ObjectComponent&lt;/code&gt;s it read (&lt;code&gt;inputs&lt;/code&gt;) and wrote (&lt;code&gt;outputs&lt;/code&gt;). An output has only one producing &lt;code&gt;CodeRun&lt;/code&gt;, and a &lt;code&gt;CodeRun&lt;/code&gt; cannot read anything produced downstream of its own outputs.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CodeRepoRelease&lt;/strong&gt;: Marks that an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt; is an official release of model code, with a &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;version&lt;/code&gt; (unique together) and an optional &lt;code&gt;website&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="fair-objects"&gt;FAIR objects&lt;a class="anchor" href="#fair-objects"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;pre class="mermaid" style="background-color: white"&gt;graph LR;&#10; O(Object) -- storage_location --&amp;gt; SL(StorageLocation)&#10; SL -- storage_root --&amp;gt; SR(StorageRoot)&#10; O -- file_type --&amp;gt; FT(FileType)&#10; O -- authors --&amp;gt; A(Author)&#10; UA(UserAuthor) -- author --&amp;gt; A&#10; OC(ObjectComponent) -- object --&amp;gt; O&#10; OC -- issues --&amp;gt; I(Issue)&#10; L(Licence) -- object --&amp;gt; O&#10; K(Keyword) -- object --&amp;gt; O&#10; KV(KeyValue) -- object --&amp;gt; O&#10; QC(QualityControlled) -- object --&amp;gt; O&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object&lt;/strong&gt;: The core traceability record behind every file: &lt;code&gt;DataProduct&lt;/code&gt;s, code repositories, configurations and submission scripts all point to an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;. It has a &lt;code&gt;uuid&lt;/code&gt;, an optional &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt;, and optionally a &lt;code&gt;StorageLocation&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;FileType&lt;/code&gt; and a list of &lt;code&gt;Author&lt;/code&gt;s.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ObjectComponent&lt;/strong&gt;: A named part of an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;, such as a table within a file. These are what &lt;code&gt;CodeRun&lt;/code&gt;s read and write. Each &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt; automatically gets a component called &lt;code&gt;whole_object&lt;/code&gt; (with &lt;code&gt;whole_object&lt;/code&gt; set to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;) that represents the whole object.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Issue&lt;/strong&gt;: A quality issue attached to one or more &lt;code&gt;ObjectComponent&lt;/code&gt;s, with a &lt;code&gt;severity&lt;/code&gt; (larger is more severe) and a &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt;. An issue with a whole object is attached to its &lt;code&gt;whole_object&lt;/code&gt; component.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;StorageLocation&lt;/strong&gt;: The location of a file, given as a &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; relative to a &lt;code&gt;StorageRoot&lt;/code&gt;, with the SHA-1 &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; of the file and whether it is &lt;code&gt;public&lt;/code&gt;. A file is stored once per &lt;code&gt;StorageRoot&lt;/code&gt;: the combination of &lt;code&gt;storage_root&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;public&lt;/code&gt; is unique.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;StorageRoot&lt;/strong&gt;: The root of a store where files are kept, given as a URI such as &lt;code&gt;https://somewebsite.com/&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;file:///someroot/&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;github://org:repo@sha/&lt;/code&gt;, and whether it is &lt;code&gt;local&lt;/code&gt;. Appending a &lt;code&gt;StorageLocation&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; to the &lt;code&gt;root&lt;/code&gt; gives the full address of the file.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FileType&lt;/strong&gt;: The &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;extension&lt;/code&gt; of a type of file, &lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;Comma-separated values file&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;csv&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Author&lt;/strong&gt;: A creator of an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;, with a &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt; and/or an &lt;code&gt;identifier&lt;/code&gt; (such as an ORCID or ROR ID).&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UserAuthor&lt;/strong&gt;: Links a registry user to the &lt;code&gt;Author&lt;/code&gt; that represents them.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licence&lt;/strong&gt;: The licence of an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;, as free text (&lt;code&gt;licence_info&lt;/code&gt;) and optionally an &lt;code&gt;identifier&lt;/code&gt; URL.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keyword&lt;/strong&gt;: A &lt;code&gt;keyphrase&lt;/code&gt; describing an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt; the keywords of a paper, optionally with the &lt;code&gt;identifier&lt;/code&gt; of an ontology term.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KeyValue&lt;/strong&gt;: Free metadata about an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt; as a &lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; and a &lt;code&gt;value&lt;/code&gt;, with each key used once per &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QualityControlled&lt;/strong&gt;: Marks that an &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt; has been quality controlled, pointing to the &lt;code&gt;Object&lt;/code&gt; of the quality control &lt;code&gt;document&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="internal-provenance"&gt;Internal provenance&lt;a class="anchor" href="#internal-provenance"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Every table also records who last changed each record (&lt;code&gt;updated_by&lt;/code&gt;) and when (&lt;code&gt;last_updated&lt;/code&gt;). These fields are set by the registry and cannot be written through the API.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Terminology</title><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/terminology/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/disabled/API/python/terminology/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="terminology-used-in-this-document"&gt;Terminology used in this document&lt;a class="anchor" href="#terminology-used-in-this-document"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;dl&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;datum&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;A specific value, encoded in a particular way, that travels through the data pipeline.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;config.yaml&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;A file (potentially with a different name) used by the data pipeline to allow users to override default pipeline behaviour. See the File API specification for more details.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;metadata.yaml&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;A file used by the data pipeline to describe available data files, listing their associated metadata. See the File API specification for more details.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;access.yaml&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;A file (potentially with a different name) generated by the data pipeline API to record file access. See the File API specification for more details.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;/dl&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="metadata"&gt;Metadata&lt;a class="anchor" href="#metadata"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;dl&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;data_product&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Identifies which kind of quantity a datum represents (e.g. “human/mixing-matrix”). Path-formatted to permit structure in the filename scheme (defined below). The desired data_product is typically specified in model code, and it is a core part of the data identifiers used in config.yaml, metadata.yaml, and access.yaml.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;version&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;A semver identifying a version of a data_product (the file API will select the most recent version if this is not specified).&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;component&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Identifies a part of a data_product.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;filename&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies the path to a file, typically relative to the data root. Only required on read, and typically inferred from metadata.yaml.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;extension&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies the extension of a file. Required on write to generate a standard filename. Typically provided by a datatype API.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;run_id&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies a unique identifier for a model run. Required on write to generate a standard filename, typically generated by the file API.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;verified_hash&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies a &amp;ldquo;verified good” SHA1 hash for a file. Used by the file API to verify file contents. Typically defined in metadata.yaml.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;calculated_hash&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies the SHA1 hash computed by the file API for a file. Typically only defined in access.yaml.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;dt&gt;max_warning&lt;/dt&gt;&#10;&lt;dd&gt;Specifies the maximum known warning level for a particular datum. Could be used by the file API to filter “bad” data (currently not supported). Typically defined in metadata.yaml.&lt;/dd&gt;&#10;&lt;/dl&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="filenames"&gt;Filenames&lt;a class="anchor" href="#filenames"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;{data root}/{data_product}&amp;hellip;/{run_id}.{extension}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Provenance Report</title><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/prov_report/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/prov_report/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="provenance-report"&gt;Provenance Report&lt;a class="anchor" href="#provenance-report"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To address the &lt;a href="https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/use_cases/#use-case-12-actor-wants-to-understand-provenance-of-reported-results"&gt;use case&lt;/a&gt; of tracing reported results back to the evidence behind them, the data registry can produce a provenance report for each data product.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Provenance is the documented history of the processes in a digital object&amp;rsquo;s lifecycle. The registry&amp;rsquo;s reports use the &lt;a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;PROV Ontology&lt;/a&gt; (PROV-O), which describes provenance in terms of:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;entities&lt;/strong&gt;: things, such as data products, external sources, code, configurations and scripts&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;activities&lt;/strong&gt;: things that happened, here code runs&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;agents&lt;/strong&gt;: the people and organisations responsible, here authors and the users who ran the code&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Provenance reports are available for &lt;code&gt;DataProduct&lt;/code&gt;s through the REST API, at &lt;code&gt;api/prov-report/&amp;lt;id&amp;gt;/&lt;/code&gt; where &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;id&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; is the data product&amp;rsquo;s id, &lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>RO Crate Objects</title><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/ro_crate/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/data_registry/ro_crate/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="research-object-crate-ro-crate"&gt;Research Object Crate (RO-Crate)&lt;a class="anchor" href="#research-object-crate-ro-crate"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href="https://www.researchobject.org/ro-crate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Research Object Crate&lt;/a&gt; (RO-Crate) packages research data together with the metadata that describes it, in a single folder or zip file with a machine-readable description, &lt;code&gt;ro-crate-metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;. The data registry can produce an RO-Crate for any data product or code run, so that results can be shared or archived together with their provenance: the code that made them, the inputs it read and where those came from.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/coderun/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/coderun/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="javadatapipeline-coderun"&gt;javaDataPipeline Coderun&lt;a class="anchor" href="#javadatapipeline-coderun"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The main class used to interface with the FAIR DataPipeline in Java, is the &lt;code&gt;Coderun&lt;/code&gt; class.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Users should initialise the &lt;code&gt;Coderun&lt;/code&gt; instance using a &lt;em&gt;try-with-resources&lt;/em&gt; block or ensure that &lt;code&gt;.close()&lt;/code&gt; is explicitly called upon finishing.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;Coderun&lt;/code&gt; constructor needs a Path to the config.yaml, a Path to the script.sh, and the registry authentication token.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The user then would access the input data product(s) using &lt;code&gt;coderun.get_dp_for_read(dataproduct_name)&lt;/code&gt;&#10;and output data product(s) using &lt;code&gt;coderun.get_dp_for_write(dataproduct_name, extension)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/issues/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/issues/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="javadatapipeline-issues"&gt;javaDataPipeline Issues&lt;a class="anchor" href="#javadatapipeline-issues"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Issues can be attached to Object_components, as well as to the Submission Script, Config File, and Code Repo.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Issues can be created and then linked to the elements that they apply to, or they can be raised directly on the element it refers to.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is an example of the creation then linking of an Issue to components, Script, and Code Repo:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-Java" data-lang="Java"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;configPath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;scriptPath&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Data_product_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;get_dp_for_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;existing/dpname&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Object_component_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;oc1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;comp1&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Object_component_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;oc2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;comp2&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Issue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;raise_issue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;#34;A serious issue&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;add_components&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;oc1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;oc2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;add_fileObject&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getScript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;coderun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;getCode_repo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And here is an example of raising an issue directly with a component and a Script:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/parameters/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/parameters/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="parameters"&gt;Parameters&lt;a class="anchor" href="#parameters"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Below are examples of all the parameter types that can be written to and read from the FAIR Data Pipeline TOML parameter file format.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Samples&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-Java" data-lang="Java"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;samples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableSamples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;addSamples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;object_component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;writeSamples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;samples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Distribution (Gamma)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-Java" data-lang="Java"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;distribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;internalShape&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;internalScale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;internalType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;DistributionType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;gamma&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;object_component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;writeDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;distribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Categorical Distribution&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-Java" data-lang="Java"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;firstMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isLowerInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isUpperInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;lowerBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;upperBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;secondMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isLowerInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isUpperInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;lowerBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;upperBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;thirdMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isLowerInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isUpperInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;lowerBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;upperBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;14&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;MinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fourthMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isLowerInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;isUpperInclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;lowerBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;upperBoundary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;categoricalDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ImmutableDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;builder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;internalType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;DistributionType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;categorical&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;bins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;firstMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;secondMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;thirdMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fourthMinMax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;weights&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;build&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;object_component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;writeDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;categoricalDistribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Estimate&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/netcdf/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/netcdf/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="netcdf"&gt;netCDF&lt;a class="anchor" href="#netcdf"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.unidata.ucar.edu/software/netcdf/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;netCDF&lt;/a&gt; is the recommended format for structured data such as arrays and tables. Like any file that is not a TOML parameter file, a netCDF file is read or written whole, through one unnamed &lt;code&gt;Object_component&lt;/code&gt;, using a netCDF library such as &lt;a href="https://docs.unidata.ucar.edu/netcdf-java/current/userguide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;NetCDF-Java&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Writing, with the file type &lt;code&gt;nc&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; try (var coderun = new Coderun(configPath, scriptPath, token)) {&#10; Data_product_write dp = coderun.get_dp_for_write(dataProduct, &amp;#34;nc&amp;#34;);&#10; Object_component_write oc = dp.getComponent();&#10; Path p = oc.writeLink();&#10; write_my_netcdf_data_to_path(p);&#10; }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;And reading:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/run/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/run/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="running-your-code"&gt;Running your code&lt;a class="anchor" href="#running-your-code"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Below is a brief explanation how to make use of the Java FAIRDataPipeline library and actually getting your code to run from the &lt;a href="https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/cli/"&gt;FAIR CLI&lt;/a&gt; command line interface. The actual command to run your Java code is given in the &lt;code&gt;script:&lt;/code&gt; line in the &lt;em&gt;config.yaml&lt;/em&gt;. In my case I run the Java code using &lt;code&gt;gradle run --args &amp;quot;${{CONFIG_DIR}}&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;. You&amp;rsquo;ll have to change this if you don&amp;rsquo;t use gradle.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/debug/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.fairdatapipeline.org/docs/api/java/debug/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="debugging--troubleshooting"&gt;Debugging / troubleshooting&lt;a class="anchor" href="#debugging--troubleshooting"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="logger"&gt;Logger&lt;a class="anchor" href="#logger"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The javaDataPipeline library uses &lt;em&gt;SLF4J&lt;/em&gt; (Simple Logging Facade for Java).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You can either use this with the SLF4J simple logger, or it can bind to your own favourite logging framework.&#10;In order to set the default simple logger to more verbose logging:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;add the &lt;code&gt;org.slf4j:slf4j-simple&lt;/code&gt; dependency&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;set the log level:&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;System.setProperty(org.slf4j.impl.SimpleLogger.DEFAULT_LOG_LEVEL_KEY, &amp;quot;TRACE&amp;quot;);&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="running-manually"&gt;Running manually&lt;a class="anchor" href="#running-manually"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Instead of running:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;fair run src/main/resources/config.yaml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can call &lt;code&gt;fair run&lt;/code&gt; and your actual java code separately:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>